id: @(#)isa.tok 1.1 26/10/19
purpose: FCode driver for the PCI-to-ISA (or LPC) bridge of PCs
copyright: Copyright 1996-2002 Sun Microsystems, Inc.  All Rights Reserved
copyright: Copyright 2026 The OpenBoot x86 port contributors
copyright: Use is subject to license terms.

\ The ISA bus of a PC: the legacy devices at fixed addresses (serial
\ ports, keyboard controller, ...) behind the PCI-to-ISA bridge, or the
\ LPC bridge of newer chipsets.  The platform's builtin-drivers package
\ loads this driver for PCI functions of class 060100, and the platform
\ then probes the legacy devices.
\
\ Addresses follow the IEEE 1275 ISA binding: two address cells,
\ phys.hi = 1 for I/O space and 0 for memory space, and phys.lo the
\ address within the space.  The text form is "i3f8" for I/O port 3f8 and
\ "a0000" for memory address a0000.
\
\ On a PC, ISA I/O ports are processor I/O ports and ISA memory addresses
\ are processor physical addresses, so map-in returns the address itself;
\ the register access words do port I/O for port addresses.

Fcode-Version3

headerless

" isa" name
" isa" device-type
2 encode-int " #address-cells" property
1 encode-int " #size-cells" property

my-address my-space encode-phys  0 encode-int encode+  0 encode-int encode+
" reg" property

external

: decode-unit  ( adr len -- pa.lo pa.hi )
   0 >r  dup  if                                  ( adr len )
      over c@  dup ascii i =  swap ascii I =  or  if
         swap 1+ swap 1-  r> 1+ >r
      then
   then                                           ( adr' len' )
   base @ >r hex  $number  r> base !              ( n false | true )
   if  0  then  r>                                ( pa.lo pa.hi )
;
: encode-unit  ( pa.lo pa.hi -- adr len )
   base @ >r hex  swap                            ( pa.hi pa.lo )
   <# u#s drop  1 and  if  ascii i hold  then  0 u#>  ( adr len )
   r> base !
;

: map-in   ( pa.lo pa.hi len -- va )  2drop  ;
: map-out  ( va len -- )  2drop  ;

: dma-alloc  ( size -- virt )  " dma-alloc" $call-parent  ;
: dma-free   ( virt size -- )  " dma-free" $call-parent  ;
: dma-map-in  ( virt size cacheable? -- devaddr )
   " dma-map-in" $call-parent
;
: dma-map-out  ( virt devaddr size -- )  " dma-map-out" $call-parent  ;
: dma-sync  ( virt devaddr size -- )  3drop  ;

: open  ( -- ok? )  true  ;
: close  ( -- )  ;

end0
